00:32:55,660 --> 00:32:57,310
you can probably guess

571
00:32:57,310 --> 00:32:58,720
what I'll say next, can't you?

572
00:33:03,570 --> 00:33:04,480
That's right.

573
00:33:05,090 --> 00:33:06,810
The next thing I want to say is that...

574
00:33:07,930 --> 00:33:09,480
the secret to making tasty boiled crabs

575
00:33:09,770 --> 00:33:11,150
is to add Himalayan salt.

576
00:33:13,360 --> 00:33:14,860
You've got it, Sarm.

577
00:33:15,030 --> 00:33:15,480
Mm.

578
00:33:15,710 --> 00:33:16,360
Perfect!

579
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:17,260
I think it'll work.

580
00:33:17,260 --> 00:33:17,970
Trust me.

581
00:33:17,970 --> 00:33:18,880
It's good.

582
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:20,120
Isn't it?

583
00:33:20,120 --> 00:33:20,860
Mm.

584
00:33:21,270 --> 00:33:22,060
Gosh...

585
00:33:22,560 --> 00:33:23,890
I'm a goddamn genius.

586
00:33:25,120 --> 00:33:27,350
But I think you can do more.

587
00:33:27,550 --> 00:33:29,950
With the quote "I love you very much,"

588
00:33:30,250 --> 00:33:31,660
make it sound

589
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:34,140
much longer.

590
00:33:35,260 --> 00:33:36,800
It'll make it even better.

591
00:33:36,940 --> 00:33:37,630
Really?

592
00:33:37,970 --> 00:33:38,470
Of course.

593
00:33:38,470 --> 00:33:39,920
Won't it sound over the top?

594
00:33:40,060 --> 00:33:40,960
I don't think so.

595
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:42,380
It'll sound more natural,

596
00:33:42,800 --> 00:33:44,180
for someone like you, that is.

597
00:33:47,430 --> 00:33:48,460
Are you taking a shot at me?

598
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:50,180
No, you're imagining it.

599
00:33:55,250 --> 00:33:56,000
Gosh.

600
00:33:57,230 --> 00:34:00,200
♫You're my love battery♫

601
00:34:00,220 --> 00:34:02,840
♫I've never been someone's priority♫

602
00:34:02,860 --> 00:34:05,570
♫Always been through heartbreak endlessly♫

603
00:34:05,590 --> 00:34:07,190
"I love you, Little Jam."

604
00:34:09,110 --> 00:34:10,060
Smooch.

605
00:34:14,570 --> 00:34:15,690
This heart is yours.

606
00:34:17,489 --> 00:34:22,300
♫Filling this heart
that once felt empty inside♫

607
00:34:22,320 --> 00:34:27,690
♫The positive vibe
in my life whenever I'm tired♫

608
00:34:27,710 --> 00:34:30,960
♫Just having you near…♫

609
00:34:49,650 --> 00:34:51,710
Where are you taking me to?

610
00:34:52,480 --> 00:34:53,920
Today,

611
00:34:56,860 --> 00:34:59,000
I'll take you scuba diving
to see the beautiful coral

612
00:34:59,020 --> 00:35:01,180
and sea anemones.

613
00:35:01,410 --> 00:35:04,450
Then, we'll have a wonderful lunch.

614
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:06,880
Mind you, the restaurant has amazing reviews.

615
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,420
Then, we'll take a nap...

616
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:10,450
recharging ourselves a bit.

617
00:35:10,470 --> 00:35:11,530
Uh...

618
00:35:11,580 --> 00:35:14,110
Once the sun goes down a bit,
we'll hike in the woods

619
00:35:14,140 --> 00:35:15,840
and watch a breathtaking sunset!

620
00:35:17,290 --> 00:35:18,360
But right now,

621
00:35:18,520 --> 00:35:19,850
let's get something to eat.

622
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:21,780
An army marches on its stomach.

623
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:27,110
And...

624
00:35:28,090 --> 00:35:30,310
What about the banana boat and parasailing?

625
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:32,070
I want to try them both.

626
00:35:33,510 --> 00:35:34,780
How about tomorrow?

627
00:35:35,530 --> 00:35:36,660
Not today?

628
00:35:36,880 --> 00:35:38,890
How about changing the afternoon nap

629
00:35:39,100 --> 00:35:41,050
to parasailing instead?

630
00:35:45,030 --> 00:35:46,360
Not a great idea, Jam.

631
00:35:46,390 --> 00:35:47,290
It goes against my plan.

632
00:35:47,460 --> 00:35:48,640
What plan?

633
00:35:49,210 --> 00:35:49,860
Well...

634
00:35:51,110 --> 00:35:52,990
Well, the hiking.

635
00:35:54,380 --> 00:35:55,190
Hm...

636
00:35:55,220 --> 00:35:56,000
Uh...

637
00:35:56,020 --> 00:35:56,690
But

638
00:35:56,710 --> 00:35:59,690
I'll take you for extreme activities
all over the island tomorrow.

639
00:35:59,710 --> 00:36:01,690
You can do everything you want.

640
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:02,890
Okay?

641
00:36:05,660 --> 00:36:06,820
Are you sure?

642
00:36:07,110 --> 00:36:07,860
Mm.

643
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:09,690
Mm,

644
00:36:09,900 --> 00:36:10,800
alright, then.

645
00:36:11,490 --> 00:36:12,950
That's so sweet of you.

646
00:36:17,440 --> 00:36:18,490
Let's have a meal, then.

647
00:36:33,670 --> 00:36:35,290
I don't want to have a meal now.

648
00:36:36,250 --> 00:36:37,660
I want to have you.

649
00:36:39,580 --> 00:36:41,290
It's like what they say,

650
00:36:42,600 --> 00:36:44,290
jam goes well with anything.

651
00:36:46,020 --> 00:36:47,220
Hey!

652
00:36:47,870 --> 00:36:49,310
We are having a meal, right?

653
00:36:56,180 --> 00:36:56,890
Let's go.

654
00:37:00,490 --> 00:37:02,580
Where are you taking me to?

655
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:03,910
Hey! Stop.

656
00:37:03,930 --> 00:37:05,270
Stop...

657
00:37:05,580 --> 00:37:06,490
Stop it!

658
00:37:12,490 --> 00:37:13,690
Here, Little Jam.

659
00:37:13,950 --> 00:37:14,670
Thank you.

660
00:37:14,670 --> 00:37:15,200
Come here.

661
00:37:16,090 --> 00:37:16,960
Here.

662
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:22,600
Slowly, okay?

663
00:37:22,600 --> 00:37:23,500
- Be careful.
- Right.

664
00:37:26,430 --> 00:37:27,270
Right here.

665
00:37:39,560 --> 00:37:40,470
Here we are.

666
00:37:40,470 --> 00:37:41,670
- Right...
- Yay.

667
00:37:43,620 --> 00:37:44,560
Be careful, alright?

668
00:37:44,780 --> 00:37:46,520
If something happens to you,

669
00:37:46,660 --> 00:37:47,540
my heart will break.

670
00:37:50,890 --> 00:37:52,090
See that over there?

671
00:37:52,090 --> 00:37:52,860
Isn't it beautiful?

672
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:54,470
That island over there?

673
00:37:54,490 --> 00:37:55,690
Yes.

674
00:37:57,300 --> 00:37:58,090
Hey...

675
00:37:58,210 --> 00:37:59,140
Mr. Sarm.

676
00:37:59,140 --> 00:37:59,560
Hm?

677
00:37:59,560 --> 00:38:01,070
I looked so goofy.

678
00:38:01,130 --> 00:38:02,550
How so, Little Jam?

679
00:38:02,810 --> 00:38:03,400
Take a look.

680
00:38:03,420 --> 00:38:04,450
- In every way.
- See?

681
00:38:04,950 --> 00:38:06,290
You look really adorable, Little Jam.

682
00:38:06,320 --> 00:38:07,150
I'll

683
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:09,280
make a print that covers the whole wall,

684
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:11,120
and I'll display it behind the bed

685
00:38:11,220 --> 00:38:12,990
so I get to see your face every day.

686
00:38:13,520 --> 00:38:14,300
I'm serious.

687
00:38:14,780 --> 00:38:16,090
Thinking about it already makes me happy.

688
00:38:19,110 --> 00:38:20,140
Ridiculous.

689
00:38:23,900 --> 00:38:24,450
Here.

690
00:38:24,620 --> 00:38:25,940
Let me take photos of you instead.

691
00:38:25,940 --> 00:38:26,710
Oh, okay.

692
00:38:29,010 --> 00:38:29,380
Alright, alright.

693
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:30,190
Let me pose real quick.

694
00:38:30,220 --> 00:38:30,820
Alright.

695
00:38:32,140 --> 00:38:33,370
Make sure you look handsome, okay?

696
00:38:33,390 --> 00:38:34,060
I already am.

697
00:38:35,600 --> 00:38:36,300
Three,

698
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:36,890
two,

699
00:38:36,890 --> 00:38:37,480
one.

700
00:38:41,450 --> 00:38:42,170
How is it?

701
00:38:42,190 --> 00:38:44,840
Am I handsome enough
to be the man of your heart?

702
00:38:46,010 --> 00:38:47,210
Mm...

703
00:38:48,510 --> 00:38:49,940
I think the likes of you

704
00:38:50,120 --> 00:38:51,790
work better as the bad guy
against my heart.

705
00:38:51,790 --> 00:38:53,070
Oh, Little Jam.

706
00:38:53,260 --> 00:38:54,710
If I were a bad guy,

707
00:38:54,710 --> 00:38:56,190
I'd be the one...

708
00:38:56,470 --> 00:38:57,890
who loves you deeply,

709
00:38:58,490 --> 00:39:00,890
from the very bottom of my heart.

710
00:39:02,290 --> 00:39:03,430
The very bottom of your heart?

711
00:39:03,430 --> 00:39:04,310
Yes.

712
00:39:04,480 --> 00:39:05,950
Now, now, let's take more selfies.

713
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:09,050
Three,

714
00:39:09,050 --> 00:39:09,390
two,

715
00:39:09,390 --> 00:39:09,880
one.

716
00:39:12,250 --> 00:39:12,730
Hm.

717
00:39:14,170 --> 00:39:16,650
My cheek will get bruised at this point.

718
00:39:18,590 --> 00:39:18,870
Ha, ha.

719
00:39:18,870 --> 00:39:20,080
It won't get bruised that easily.

720
00:39:23,010 --> 00:39:24,020
Mm...

721
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:26,120
Oh...

722
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:28,570
Shooting from every angle.

723
00:39:30,010 --> 00:39:31,660
Are you a vacuum cleaner or what?

724
00:39:31,660 --> 00:39:32,270
Yes...

725
00:39:32,270 --> 00:39:33,310
Oh, Little Jam!

726
00:39:33,570 --> 00:39:34,180
Dolphins!

727
00:39:34,360 --> 00:39:35,260
- Whoa!
- Mm.

728
00:39:44,230 --> 00:39:45,880
Shooting in 360 degrees.

729
00:39:46,060 --> 00:39:47,260
We'll get shots from every angle.

730
00:39:48,130 --> 00:39:48,690
Ha, ha.

731
00:39:48,690 --> 00:39:50,320
You teased me again.

732
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:02,860
What?!

733
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:03,670
Little Jam,

734
00:40:03,800 --> 00:40:05,050
what's that box?

735
00:40:05,260 --> 00:40:05,680
A box?

736
00:40:05,680 --> 00:40:06,990
Over there. Right there.

737
00:40:07,450 --> 00:40:08,730
Maybe there's something in it.

738
00:40:08,970 --> 00:40:10,310
Maybe it's a treasure.

739
00:40:10,530 --> 00:40:11,620
Go pick it up.

740
00:40:11,790 --> 00:40:12,890
Come on, Little Jam.

741
00:40:12,960 --> 00:40:14,100
I would rather not.

742
00:40:16,020 --> 00:40:16,640
It's okay.

743
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:17,510
If that's the case, I'll...

744
00:40:17,650 --> 00:40:18,460
I'll... I'll...

745
00:40:19,110 --> 00:40:20,560
Let us not, Mr. Sarm.

746
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:22,060
In movies, they say...

747
00:40:22,290 --> 00:40:24,460
we should not touch
someone else's stuff without permission.

748
00:40:25,090 --> 00:40:26,200
Come on, it's okay.

749
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:28,880
You would be in trouble
if the owner came back and looked for it.

750
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:29,480
Maybe it's not...

751
00:40:29,480 --> 00:40:31,660
There are no shamans here either.

752
00:40:32,830 --> 00:40:34,870
Little Jam, there's nobody here, though.

753
00:40:34,870 --> 00:40:35,390
Take a peek inside the box...

754
00:40:35,390 --> 00:40:36,310
Exactly.

755
00:40:36,310 --> 00:40:37,360
There is nobody here.

756
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:38,860
And your feng shui master

757
00:40:38,860 --> 00:40:40,430
is back in Pak Chong.

758
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:42,010
He cannot save you in time.

759
00:40:42,710 --> 00:40:43,920
Just open it for a second.

760
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:44,480
It's okay, we'll...

761
00:40:44,480 --> 00:40:44,990
No!

762
00:40:46,190 --> 00:40:46,920
Let us not.

763
00:40:47,450 --> 00:40:48,240
But...

764
00:40:48,870 --> 00:40:49,470
Just a quick peek.

765
00:40:49,470 --> 00:40:50,670
No, stop it, Mr. Sarm!

766
00:40:50,670 --> 00:40:51,210
Try...

767
00:40:51,210 --> 00:40:51,930
If you open it,

768
00:40:51,930 --> 00:40:53,510
we will break up.

769
00:40:55,490 --> 00:40:56,590
But, Little Jam...

770
00:40:57,190 --> 00:40:58,480
Not even a quick peek?

771
00:41:01,550 --> 00:41:03,120
But...

772
00:41:04,270 --> 00:41:04,830
Oh...

773
00:41:04,830 --> 00:41:05,800
You're right, Little Jam.

774
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:07,190
Who knows what's inside that box.

775
00:41:07,190 --> 00:41:08,860
If there's something dangerous inside,

776
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:10,170
- nobody can save us, right?
- Yes.

777
00:41:10,170 --> 00:41:11,010
Let's leave it there.

778
00:41:11,260 --> 00:41:12,650
Also, it is getting dark.

779
00:41:12,650 --> 00:41:13,090
Mm.

780
00:41:13,090 --> 00:41:14,240
Let us head back, shall we?

781
00:41:14,240 --> 00:41:15,030
Yeah, there are swarms of mosquitoes, too.

782
00:41:15,030 --> 00:41:15,800
Let's get going, then.

783
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:16,440
- Let us.
- Mm.

784
00:41:17,950 --> 00:41:18,880
Little Jam...

785
00:41:26,510 --> 00:41:28,060
I got you a surprise.

786
00:41:29,070 --> 00:41:29,760
Gosh...

787
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:32,320
I even styled
my hair to look this cool.

788
00:41:33,190 --> 00:41:34,060
There goes my plan.

789
00:41:34,530 --> 00:41:35,510
Little Jam.

790
00:41:35,750 --> 00:41:36,640
Mr. Sarm!

791
00:41:36,640 --> 00:41:37,800
Hurry up, Mr. Sarm!

792
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:38,860
Okay, Little Jam.

793
00:41:39,110 --> 00:41:40,060
Wait for me.

794
00:41:40,060 --> 00:41:40,850
I'm on my way.

795
00:41:42,460 --> 00:41:43,120
Hey.

796
00:41:43,550 --> 00:41:44,730
Get out of there already, Mr. Sarm...

797
00:41:51,490 --> 00:41:52,570
Mr. Sarm!

798
00:41:53,420 --> 00:41:54,000
Yes?

799
00:41:54,310 --> 00:41:55,280
Let us get going.

800
00:41:58,140 --> 00:41:59,630
Quickly, Mr. Sarm!

801
00:41:59,630 --> 00:42:00,670
It is getting dark.

802
00:42:00,670 --> 00:42:01,430
Okay, okay.

803
00:42:01,430 --> 00:42:02,080
I'm coming.

804
00:42:02,210 --> 00:42:03,010
Little Jam...

805
00:42:17,260 --> 00:42:23,260
[Uncle Mai's Kitchen]

806
00:42:23,400 --> 00:42:24,210
Little Jam,

807
00:42:24,230 --> 00:42:24,790
look.

808
00:42:24,810 --> 00:42:26,110
I have dinner prepared for us.

809
00:42:26,130 --> 00:42:27,110
It looks so delicious.

810
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:28,040
Are you hungry?

811
00:42:28,060 --> 00:42:29,060
You are, aren't you?

812
00:42:29,080 --> 00:42:30,440
Let's have dinner, then.

813
00:42:30,460 --> 00:42:31,110
Come on.

814
00:42:31,660 --> 00:42:33,470
Wow...

815
00:42:33,470 --> 00:42:34,830
Ta-da, ta-da...

816
00:42:34,830 --> 00:42:36,310
Dun-dun, ta-da, ta-da

817
00:42:36,310 --> 00:42:36,790
Da-da

818
00:42:36,790 --> 00:42:38,860
I have to leave early tomorrow.

819
00:42:43,070 --> 00:42:45,250
I cannot stay any longer.

820
00:42:46,790 --> 00:42:50,050
Mr. Sib's client flew here
from Hong Kong with his family,

821
00:42:50,390 --> 00:42:52,060
and he wants me to host them.

822
00:43:05,510 --> 00:43:06,460
But...

823
00:43:10,870 --> 00:43:12,750
Isn't tomorrow your day off, Little Jam?

824
00:43:13,660 --> 00:43:15,240
We also have plans.

825
00:43:17,130 --> 00:43:18,130
Oh, right.

826
00:43:18,130 --> 00:43:20,280
Sib has many secretaries.

827
00:43:21,150 --> 00:43:22,750
Can't he let one of them
handle the job?

828
00:43:26,990 --> 00:43:30,810
I already hosted the client's family,

829
00:43:32,160 --> 00:43:34,640
so I knew

830
00:43:35,260 --> 00:43:36,890
what he liked

831
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:40,600
and what his wife
and kids were allergic to.

832
00:43:50,430 --> 00:43:51,270
And...

833
00:43:53,470 --> 00:43:54,810
Can't you stay, Little Jam?

834
00:44:19,390 --> 00:44:21,090
Do you see these raindrops?

835
00:44:23,710 --> 00:44:24,460
They...

836
00:44:25,310 --> 00:44:26,670
They're my teardrops.

837
00:44:37,090 --> 00:44:38,310
Mr. Sarm...

838
00:44:39,480 --> 00:44:41,260
I cannot say no to Mr. Sib.

839
00:45:19,210 --> 00:45:20,530
Can I come with you, then?

840
00:45:23,770 --> 00:45:24,460
Please?

841
00:45:24,790 --> 00:45:25,660
Can I come with you?

842
00:45:35,940 --> 00:45:37,630
That is not possible.

843
00:45:43,250 --> 00:45:44,630
Can you not leave, Little Jam?

844
00:45:47,260 --> 00:45:49,310
It's really hard to find time

845
00:45:49,310 --> 00:45:50,490
for a trip together.

846
00:45:55,770 --> 00:45:58,450
You can stay here and enjoy the vacation.

847
00:46:00,870 --> 00:46:02,050
Without you here,

848
00:46:03,340 --> 00:46:05,230
this place means nothing.

849
00:46:06,150 --> 00:46:07,160
I'm not staying.

850
00:46:12,720 --> 00:46:14,270
It's tomorrow no matter what, right?

851
00:46:19,970 --> 00:46:20,860
Mm.

852
00:46:22,790 --> 00:46:23,410
Oh, oh.

853
00:46:23,410 --> 00:46:24,460
Mr. Sarm...

854
00:46:27,400 --> 00:46:29,070
If my life were a soap opera,

855
00:46:29,490 --> 00:46:30,990
it'd be called

856
00:46:31,490 --> 00:46:33,110
"Traiphop's Tears."

857
00:46:33,710 --> 00:46:35,040
The antagonist

858
00:46:35,150 --> 00:46:36,460
would be none other

859
00:46:36,630 --> 00:46:38,310
than my own older brother.

860
00:46:39,110 --> 00:46:41,830
He assigned the task
at such perfect timing.

861
00:47:05,050 --> 00:47:06,760
You returned earlier than expected.

862
00:47:10,190 --> 00:47:11,850
Can you prepare gotu kola tea for me?

863
00:47:12,080 --> 00:47:13,480
Make me a full pot.

864
00:47:14,710 --> 00:47:15,770
I'll come back here to enjoy it.

865
00:47:16,720 --> 00:47:17,440
No problem.

866
00:47:36,080 --> 00:47:37,510
Right. Jab and use your hips.

867
00:47:37,510 --> 00:47:38,310
Try jabbing.

868
00:47:39,120 --> 00:47:39,850
Good.

869
00:47:40,850 --> 00:47:41,730
That's good.

870
00:47:43,290 --> 00:47:43,870
Not like that.

871
00:47:44,040 --> 00:47:44,570
Oh?

872
00:47:45,280 --> 00:47:46,060
Mr. Sarm,

873
00:47:46,360 --> 00:47:49,060
did you change your mind
and come back to welcome our new boxers?

874
00:47:50,790 --> 00:47:51,810
Not exactly.

875
00:47:52,490 --> 00:47:53,790
How many boxers are in this batch?

876
00:47:53,790 --> 00:47:55,280
Two, actually.

877
00:47:55,550 --> 00:47:56,710
But don't worry,

878
00:47:56,800 --> 00:47:59,240
we've got both an amateur
and a professional.

879
00:47:59,260 --> 00:48:00,200
They're all talented.

880
00:48:00,200 --> 00:48:01,510
They're not hard to train.

881
00:48:02,320 --> 00:48:03,600
By the way, Mr. Sarm,

882
00:48:03,600 --> 00:48:05,080
aren't you going to give
them a welcome match?

883
00:48:05,490 --> 00:48:07,160
Let them shine on their own.

884
00:48:07,550 --> 00:48:09,110
You've got a great body,

885
00:48:09,110 --> 00:48:11,130
and everyone in Pak Chong knows that

886
00:48:11,130 --> 00:48:12,770
you're the real deal.

887
00:48:15,650 --> 00:48:16,410
Fine.

888
00:48:16,500 --> 00:48:17,230
I'll hop in.

889
00:48:17,720 --> 00:48:18,300
See you soon.

890
00:49:10,980 --> 00:49:13,980
[My Little Jam]

891
00:49:32,090 --> 00:49:33,690
A smartphone can be charged,

892
00:49:34,590 --> 00:49:35,530
but look at me.

893
00:49:38,070 --> 00:49:39,310
Nobody's charging my heart.

894
00:49:58,690 --> 00:49:59,840
Gosh...

895
00:50:09,620 --> 00:50:10,850
[I arrived safe and sound

896
00:50:10,880 --> 00:50:12,340
Do not worry; I will be busy working

897
00:50:12,370 --> 00:50:13,470
Might not get to answer your calls]

898
00:50:16,490 --> 00:50:22,600
[My Little Jam]

899
00:50:25,070 --> 00:50:26,200
[Sarm: Hey]

900
00:50:26,230 --> 00:50:27,550
[Sarm: Still occupied? What are you doing?
Have you eaten yet?]

901
00:50:27,570 --> 00:50:28,500
[Sarm: I'm home, actually;
I left soon after you did

902
00:50:28,530 --> 00:50:29,190
Being there alone felt too empty]

903
00:50:29,210 --> 00:50:30,180
[Sarm: I had fun boxing today;
I got destroyed by a pro

904
00:50:30,210 --> 00:50:31,290
It all hurts, but it's not as bad as
not seeing you, Little Jam]

905
00:50:31,320 --> 00:50:32,510
[Sarm: Take care of yourself over there,
eat lots of good food,

906
00:50:32,530 --> 00:50:33,400
get plenty of rest, and don't overwork;
I'm worried about you]

907
00:50:33,880 --> 00:50:34,570
Whoa!

908
00:50:35,760 --> 00:50:36,690
You're looking at me?

909
00:50:37,210 --> 00:50:39,050
You look at me every day, huh?

910
00:50:40,310 --> 00:50:41,260
Look at the wall instead.

911
00:50:58,640 --> 00:51:00,460
You seem troubled,

912
00:51:00,910 --> 00:51:02,480
as if you've had
a fight with your partner.

913
00:51:04,870 --> 00:51:05,840
Mr. Sib...

914
00:51:07,360 --> 00:51:08,860
You are not the real Mr. Sib.

915
00:51:09,040 --> 00:51:11,010
Give me back my real boss.

916
00:51:12,260 --> 00:51:13,430
I'll ask you again.

917
00:51:14,010 --> 00:51:15,480
What's troubling your mind?

918
00:51:17,130 --> 00:51:19,910
If Mr. Sarm disappeared again,

919
00:51:20,410 --> 00:51:22,060
what would you do?

920
00:51:23,470 --> 00:51:24,720
It's simple, really.

921
00:51:25,330 --> 00:51:26,960
I'll send you to find him again,

922
00:51:27,240 --> 00:51:28,370
but this time,

923
00:51:28,370 --> 00:51:29,730
if you can't find him,

924
00:51:29,870 --> 00:51:31,060
do not come back.

925
00:51:31,430 --> 00:51:33,510
Even if you have to
turn the whole world upside down,

926
00:51:33,890 --> 00:51:35,260
you have to find him.

927
00:51:35,600 --> 00:51:37,630
I have probably used up all my luck.

928
00:51:38,710 --> 00:51:39,310
Oh?

929
00:51:39,510 --> 00:51:40,400
Why is that?

930
00:51:41,750 --> 00:51:43,130
What did you do to my brother again?

931
00:51:43,480 --> 00:51:44,530
Sarm...

932
00:51:44,910 --> 00:51:46,700
He's my precious little brother.

933
00:51:48,550 --> 00:51:50,130
I have not done anything,

934
00:51:51,480 --> 00:51:52,640
but I do not understand

935
00:51:52,640 --> 00:51:55,000
why he looked that upset either.

936
00:51:57,110 --> 00:51:58,400
I just talked to my dad,

937
00:51:59,010 --> 00:52:01,120
and he said
Sarm had just gotten back from Ko Pha-ngan

938
00:52:01,360 --> 00:52:03,030
and looked sad.

939
00:52:03,280 --> 00:52:04,440
He has returned?

940
00:52:04,760 --> 00:52:05,520
Mm.

941
00:52:06,130 --> 00:52:07,180
Oh...

942
00:52:07,200 --> 00:52:09,100
You went there with him, right?

943
00:52:10,670 --> 00:52:11,690
I'm so sorry

944
00:52:11,710 --> 00:52:12,760
for asking you to come here.

945
00:52:13,290 --> 00:52:15,140
I interrupted
your time together on your trip, right?

946
00:52:15,360 --> 00:52:16,290
No, not at all.

947
00:52:16,480 --> 00:52:16,870
Uh,

948
00:52:16,870 --> 00:52:18,460
I was just on vacation.

949
00:52:20,310 --> 00:52:21,160
Here's the deal.

950
00:52:21,790 --> 00:52:23,260
How about I teach you

951
00:52:23,560 --> 00:52:25,890
how to stop saying one thing
and meaning another?

952
00:52:28,310 --> 00:52:29,770
How much is this training?

953
00:52:30,280 --> 00:52:32,480
If it is affordable, then I will sign up.

954
00:52:33,090 --> 00:52:34,600
You're good at dodging the subject.

955
00:52:35,590 --> 00:52:36,280
At any rate,

956
00:52:37,380 --> 00:52:39,720
if something is troubling you,

957
00:52:40,390 --> 00:52:41,850
don't hold it for too long.

958
00:52:42,210 --> 00:52:43,930
Don't complicate things.

959
00:52:44,600 --> 00:52:46,050
I know you're talented,

960
00:52:46,690 --> 00:52:47,590
and you already know

961
00:52:47,830 --> 00:52:49,250
what you should do.

962
00:52:50,290 --> 00:52:52,470
If I delayed things any longer,

963
00:52:52,710 --> 00:52:54,460
Mr. Sarm might lose himself.

964
00:52:54,870 --> 00:52:56,310
He might not just take a trip to an island

965
00:52:56,530 --> 00:52:58,690
but to outer space.

966
00:52:58,870 --> 00:52:59,810
Mr. Sib.

967
00:53:01,030 --> 00:53:03,310
May I go and follow my heart?

968
00:53:04,330 --> 00:53:05,260
Go ahead.

969
00:53:05,760 --> 00:53:07,520
I always support you.

970
00:53:07,920 --> 00:53:08,860
Also...

971
00:53:09,120 --> 00:53:10,280
follow it through.

972
00:53:10,770 --> 00:53:11,930
Once you reach your destination,

973
00:53:12,050 --> 00:53:13,310
do come back and tell me about it.

974
00:53:13,660 --> 00:53:14,860
Thank you, Mr. Sib!

975
00:53:14,970 --> 00:53:17,260
May your success shine

976
00:53:17,260 --> 00:53:19,040
brighter than fireworks.

977
00:53:19,170 --> 00:53:20,170
Get going already

978
00:53:20,170 --> 00:53:21,190
before it's too late.

979
00:53:21,360 --> 00:53:22,450
Right, Mr. Sib.

980
00:53:23,430 --> 00:53:24,460
I will be on my way, then.

981
00:53:33,200 --> 00:53:34,060
Song.

982
00:53:34,270 --> 00:53:35,050
Jam.

983
00:53:35,050 --> 00:53:35,710
Take a seat.

984
00:53:35,710 --> 00:53:36,460
Thank you.

985
00:53:39,270 --> 00:53:40,370
What brings you here?

986
00:53:40,370 --> 00:53:42,080
Why are you in such a rush?

987
00:53:42,320 --> 00:53:43,660
I need help.

988
00:53:44,320 --> 00:53:45,840
Sarm is mad at me,

989
00:53:45,840 --> 00:53:47,570
and I am here to make it up to him.

990
00:53:47,930 --> 00:53:49,950
Sarm is mad at you, really?

991
00:53:50,520 --> 00:53:51,010
And...

992
00:53:51,320 --> 00:53:52,730
How was the trip to Ko Pha-ngan?

993
00:53:52,920 --> 00:53:53,870
Can you tell me about it?

994
00:53:54,110 --> 00:53:56,670
An urgent task came up,
so I had to leave early.

995
00:53:56,770 --> 00:53:58,550
Mr. Sarm seemed a little upset, too.

996
00:53:58,550 --> 00:54:00,090
He did not pick up the phone

997
00:54:00,170 --> 00:54:01,660
or reply to my texts.

998
00:54:02,430 --> 00:54:03,800
And... did...

999
00:54:04,530 --> 00:54:05,550
Did Sarm...

1000
00:54:05,570 --> 00:54:07,660
Did he give you the ring?

1001
00:54:08,860 --> 00:54:09,750
The ring?

1002
00:54:10,590 --> 00:54:11,550
The ring.

1003
00:54:12,320 --> 00:54:13,530
What ring?

1004
00:54:14,690 --> 00:54:15,620
Well...

1005
00:54:16,000 --> 00:54:17,080
When...

1006
00:54:17,170 --> 00:54:18,250
someone...

1007
00:54:18,250 --> 00:54:19,530
gives another person a ring,

1008
00:54:19,800 --> 00:54:21,840
what...does that mean?

1009
00:54:22,320 --> 00:54:23,520
They want them to sell it?

1010
00:54:25,640 --> 00:54:26,690
No, no.

1011
00:54:26,690 --> 00:54:27,550
Jam...

1012
00:54:28,060 --> 00:54:29,390
Picture this.

1013
00:54:29,630 --> 00:54:30,670
If

1014
00:54:30,670 --> 00:54:32,860
someone

1015
00:54:32,860 --> 00:54:34,530
wants to give you a ring,

1016
00:54:35,040 --> 00:54:37,910
what's their intention?

1017
00:54:40,570 --> 00:54:43,450
Tick-tock, tick-tock, tick-tock.

1018
00:54:43,870 --> 00:54:45,340
To marry me?

1019
00:54:45,420 --> 00:54:46,900
Excellent, Jam!

1020
00:54:47,590 --> 00:54:48,690
The intention is to marry.

1021
00:54:48,970 --> 00:54:50,480
Now, then,

1022
00:54:50,720 --> 00:54:51,840
Sarm

1023
00:54:52,060 --> 00:54:53,770
wants to give you

1024
00:54:53,770 --> 00:54:54,840
his ring...

1025
00:54:56,010 --> 00:54:58,730
This means that he wants to...

1026
00:54:59,130 --> 00:55:01,000
He wants to marry me?

1027
00:55:01,000 --> 00:55:01,770
Well done!

1028
00:55:01,770 --> 00:55:03,810
You hit the nail on the head, Jam.

1029
00:55:04,060 --> 00:55:05,260
But that is not possible.

1030
00:55:05,410 --> 00:55:07,130
It is possible, Jam.

1031
00:55:07,920 --> 00:55:09,480
Think about it.

1032
00:55:09,830 --> 00:55:11,080
Did

1033
00:55:11,080 --> 00:55:13,440
Sarm ask you...

1034
00:55:13,660 --> 00:55:15,050
to look at a certain box?

1035
00:55:16,590 --> 00:55:17,910
What's that box?

1036
00:55:18,040 --> 00:55:18,460
A box?

1037
00:55:18,460 --> 00:55:19,660
Over there. Right there.

1038
00:55:21,130 --> 00:55:22,310
That box...

1039
00:55:23,870 --> 00:55:25,480
The one I ignored?

1040
00:55:26,040 --> 00:55:28,060
He was probably devastated that...

1041
00:55:28,250 --> 00:55:29,810
things didn't go according to plan.

1042
00:55:29,810 --> 00:55:31,240
And do you know

1043
00:55:31,530 --> 00:55:33,200
where Mr. Sarm is?

1044
00:55:33,390 --> 00:55:34,990
He's probably somewhere nearby.

1045
00:55:34,990 --> 00:55:38,090
He's probably crying so hard
that he could flood Pak Chong right now.

1046
00:55:39,190 --> 00:55:40,860
Do not wait around, Jam.

1047
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:42,930
What should I do, Song?

1048
00:55:44,470 --> 00:55:46,280
Why don't you propose back to him?

1049
00:55:46,760 --> 00:55:48,200
If he asks

1050
00:55:48,200 --> 00:55:49,280
what you brought to propose with,

1051
00:55:49,510 --> 00:55:50,670
just say,

1052
00:55:50,670 --> 00:55:52,060
"This kiss."

1053
00:55:52,410 --> 00:55:53,260
Trust me.

1054
00:55:53,560 --> 00:55:54,460
Works every time.

1055
00:55:54,460 --> 00:55:55,910
Thank you, Mr. Song.

1056
00:56:00,880 --> 00:56:02,270
You've got this, Jam.

1057
00:56:02,860 --> 00:56:03,650
He loves me!

1058
00:56:08,210 --> 00:56:09,640
He loves me not!

1059
00:56:12,960 --> 00:56:13,660
He loves me!

1060
00:56:17,540 --> 00:56:18,460
He loves me not!

1061
00:56:18,630 --> 00:56:19,660
Mr. Sarm.

1062
00:56:20,490 --> 00:56:21,470
Little...

1063
00:56:21,730 --> 00:56:22,680
Mr. Sarm.

1064
00:56:25,210 --> 00:56:26,550
I am here to make it up to you...

1065
00:56:27,590 --> 00:56:28,730
Though I am late...

1066
00:56:29,260 --> 00:56:30,460
at least I am here.

1067
00:56:33,790 --> 00:56:35,550
Do not stay quiet, Mr. Sarm.

1068
00:56:35,680 --> 00:56:37,490
You are giving me bad vibes.

1069
00:56:38,230 --> 00:56:39,430
What did I tell you to call me?

1070
00:56:40,760 --> 00:56:41,810
Sarm.

1071
00:56:43,360 --> 00:56:44,080
Didn't catch that.

1072
00:56:45,030 --> 00:56:46,290
"Sarm."

1073
00:56:55,140 --> 00:56:56,290
Why are you here?

1074
00:56:57,730 --> 00:56:59,570
I am here to apply for a position.

1075
00:57:01,890 --> 00:57:02,860
You have to go there.

1076
00:57:02,860 --> 00:57:03,840
That's the headquarters.

1077
00:57:05,030 --> 00:57:06,160
Why did you come for me?

1078
00:57:08,040 --> 00:57:10,060
I can only apply for
this position with you.

1079
00:57:11,390 --> 00:57:12,460
What position exactly?

1080
00:57:14,550 --> 00:57:16,320
It's...

1081
00:57:19,010 --> 00:57:20,860
The owner of Adisuan Farm's spouse.

1082
00:57:24,710 --> 00:57:25,690
I'm sorry, Little Jam?

1083
00:57:26,030 --> 00:57:27,240
Am I daydreaming?

1084
00:57:27,240 --> 00:57:28,290
I must be.

1085
00:57:29,720 --> 00:57:30,310
Little Jam.

1086
00:57:30,750 --> 00:57:31,320
Little Jam.

1087
00:57:31,790 --> 00:57:32,860
Slap me in the face.

1088
00:57:32,970 --> 00:57:33,910
Give me a wake-up slap.

1089
00:57:34,060 --> 00:57:35,070
This is impossible.

1090
00:57:35,260 --> 00:57:35,730
Little Jam.

1091
00:57:35,730 --> 00:57:37,270
Give me a slap. A slap, a slap...

1092
00:57:52,310 --> 00:57:53,530
Is this clear enough

1093
00:57:54,290 --> 00:57:55,330
that this is not a dream?

1094
00:57:57,810 --> 00:57:58,720
I'm almost awake now.

1095
00:58:07,660 --> 00:58:08,860
Is this clear enough?

1096
00:58:10,320 --> 00:58:11,120
Just a little more...

1097
00:58:11,260 --> 00:58:12,730
Is it clear now, Sarm?

1098
00:58:13,190 --> 00:58:14,290
Do not be so tense.

1099
00:58:15,160 --> 00:58:16,320
I am not.

1100
00:58:16,320 --> 00:58:17,260
I did it without knowing.

1101
00:58:17,450 --> 00:58:18,270
So...

1102
00:58:19,110 --> 00:58:20,010
You're making it up to me...

1103
00:58:20,330 --> 00:58:21,680
and you want to be my spouse?

1104
00:58:22,020 --> 00:58:22,610
Mm.

1105
00:58:24,170 --> 00:58:26,120
Do you accept?

1106
00:58:33,550 --> 00:58:34,290
If so...

1107
00:58:35,340 --> 00:58:37,150
show me what you've got.

1108
00:58:37,910 --> 00:58:39,040
I have none.

1109
00:58:40,170 --> 00:58:41,800
I always burn an omelet when I make one.

1110
00:58:44,860 --> 00:58:46,650
All I can make is cup noodles.

1111
00:58:51,710 --> 00:58:54,150
But I can buy you yogurt drinks.

1112
00:58:56,370 --> 00:58:57,130
And...

1113
00:58:57,930 --> 00:58:59,260
What do you want as your payment?

1114
00:59:01,490 --> 00:59:04,290
Love me and take care of me
for the rest of your life.

1115
00:59:05,610 --> 00:59:08,010
Do not terminate this contract.

1116
00:59:11,260 --> 00:59:12,460
And what will I get in return,

1117
00:59:14,200 --> 00:59:14,860
hm?

1118
00:59:17,550 --> 00:59:20,080
I will take care of you as best as I can.

1119
00:59:29,260 --> 00:59:30,630
I'll give you headaches, you know?

1120
00:59:30,890 --> 00:59:31,890
Are you cool with that?

1121
00:59:32,860 --> 00:59:34,610
I have gotten used to it by now.

1122
00:59:35,390 --> 00:59:36,890
And what about me
making a big deal out of everything?

1123
00:59:37,550 --> 00:59:38,440
I always do it.

1124
00:59:39,450 --> 00:59:41,050
You are my jam.

1125
00:59:41,520 --> 00:59:42,190
Oh...

1126
00:59:42,190 --> 00:59:42,870
It is true.

1127
00:59:43,430 --> 00:59:44,570
What about being this goofy?

1128
00:59:46,610 --> 00:59:47,530
Can you handle it?

1129
00:59:48,850 --> 00:59:50,640
No matter what you are like...

1130
00:59:51,010 --> 00:59:52,650
I will always love you.

1131
00:59:57,910 --> 00:59:59,710
So, do you accept me or not?

1132
01:00:01,970 --> 01:00:03,730
This position has always been yours.

1133
01:00:04,330 --> 01:00:05,470
You have no clue at all,

1134
01:00:05,930 --> 01:00:06,460
huh?

1135
01:00:07,660 --> 01:00:08,860
Let's get married.

1136
01:00:16,060 --> 01:00:16,930
Wait...

1137
01:00:17,120 --> 01:00:19,520
Aren't I supposed to say that?

1138
01:00:19,520 --> 01:00:20,170
And will you?

1139
01:00:20,170 --> 01:00:20,720
I will.

1140
01:00:20,860 --> 01:00:21,950
I will. I will.

1141
01:00:21,950 --> 01:00:22,330
Today.

1142
01:00:22,330 --> 01:00:22,830
Right now.

1143
